bazel/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/deployments","created_at":"2014-06-12T16:00:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T22:36:14Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T23:00:16Z","git_url":"git://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:bazelbuild/bazel.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel","homepage":"https://bazel.build","size":992874,"stargazers_count":24886,"watchers_count":24886,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4359,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1818,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1818,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\nThere is no pdb output on Windows in `cc_common.link`. This information should be added. \r\n\r\n### Feature requests: what underlying problem are you trying to solve with this feature?\r\nI need bazel rule which builds shared libraries. Rule need satisfy following properties:\r\n1) Rule provides import libraries and pdb on windows\r\n2) I can write my `BUILD` files in crossplatform style (no \".dll\" in label names)\r\n3) I can use custom names for output files (for example same label has output name foo.dll on windows and libbar.so on linux)\r\n4) It has transitive linkage\r\n\r\nSeems using `cc_common.link` in my rule is a good choice, but it does not provide pdb files as a result. \r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\nFollowing code shows that there is no pdb\r\n**my_rule.bzl**\r\n```\r\nload(\"@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:toolchain_utils.bzl\", \"find_cpp_toolchain\")\r\n\r\ndef print_val(prefix, name, type, value):\r\n    # print(\"{}.{}, type: {}, value: {}\".format(prefix, name, type, value))\r\n    print(\"{}.{} = {}\".format(prefix, name, value))\r\n \r\ndef dump(obj, prefix):\r\n    for field in dir(obj):\r\n        attr_value =  getattr(obj, field)\r\n        attr_value_type =  type(getattr(obj, field))\r\n        print_val(prefix, field, attr_value_type, attr_value)\r\n        dump2(attr_value, prefix + \".\" + field)\r\n    \r\ndef dump2(obj, prefix):        \r\n    for field in dir(obj):\r\n        attr_value =  getattr(obj, field)\r\n        attr_value_type =  type(getattr(obj, field))        \r\n        print_val(prefix, field, attr_value_type, attr_value)\r\n    \r\n\r\ndef _cc_bin_impl(ctx):\r\n    cc_toolchain = find_cpp_toolchain(ctx)\r\n    feature_configuration = cc_common.configure_features(\r\n        ctx = ctx,\r\n        cc_toolchain = cc_toolchain,\r\n        requested_features = ctx.features,\r\n        unsupported_features = ctx.disabled_features,\r\n    )\r\n    \r\n    (_compilation_context, compilation_outputs) = cc_common.compile(\r\n        name = ctx.label.name,\r\n        actions = ctx.actions,\r\n        feature_configuration = feature_configuration,\r\n        cc_toolchain = cc_toolchain,\r\n        srcs = ctx.files.srcs,\r\n        compilation_contexts = [],\r\n    )\r\n    \r\n    linking_outputs = cc_common.link(\r\n        name = ctx.label.name,\r\n        actions = ctx.actions,\r\n        feature_configuration = feature_configuration,\r\n        cc_toolchain = cc_toolchain,\r\n        language = \"c++\",\r\n        compilation_outputs = compilation_outputs,\r\n        linking_contexts = [],\r\n        user_link_flags = [],\r\n        link_deps_statically = True,\r\n        output_type = \"dynamic_library\",\r\n    )\r\n    files = []\r\n    print(\"linking_outputs content:\")\r\n    dump(linking_outputs, \"  linking_outputs\")\r\n\r\n\r\ncc_bin = rule(\r\n    implementation = _cc_bin_impl,\r\n    attrs = {\r\n        \"srcs\": attr.label_list(allow_files = [\".cc\"]),\r\n        \"_cc_toolchain\": attr.label(default = \"@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:current_cc_toolchain\"),\r\n    },\r\n    fragments = [\"cpp\"],\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**BUILD**\r\n```\r\npackage(default_visibility = [\"//visibility:public\"])\r\nload(\"//:my_rule.bzl\", \"cc_bin\")\r\n\r\ncc_bin(\r\n      name = \"bar\",\r\n      srcs = [\"main.cc\"],\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAfter building you can see:\r\n```\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:54:5: linking_outputs content:\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.executable = None\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link = <unknown object com.google.devtools.build.lib.rules.cpp.AutoValue_LibraryToLink>\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link.alwayslink = False\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link.dynamic_library = <generated file bar.dll>\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link.interface_library = None\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link.pic_static_library = None\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link.resolved_symlink_dynamic_library = None\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link.resolved_symlink_interface_library = None\r\nDEBUG: C:/git/bazel_my_examples/cc_link_no_pdb/my_rule.bzl:5:5:   linking_outputs.library_to_link.static_library = None\r\n```\r\nIt provides `linking_outputs.library_to_link.dynamic_library` with shared library but there is no information about pdb. \r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\nWindows 10 x64\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\nrelease 0.29.0rc5\r\n\r\n### Any other information, logs, or outputs that you want to share?\r\n[Another problem with cc_common_link on Windows](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/9133)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/9165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/9165/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2576745014,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjU3Njc0NTAxNA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/events/2576745014","actor":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io","html_url":"https://github.com/bazel-io","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bazel-io/received_events","type":"User","